<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Latgalians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Latgallians</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Latgalians were a Baltic tribe of eastern Latvia, settled along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-dvina">Daugava</a> and in the uplands to the east by the late first millennium. Their lands included the principalities of Jersika, Koknese and Talava, and some had become <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Christians under Rus' influence. Conquered by the German crusaders in the 13th century, they merged with neighbouring Baltic peoples into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latvians">Latvians</a>.</p></div>
